; Test: HEAD sink - limit results
; ================================
;
; Demonstrates: (O (head N <template>)) to limit output to first N results
; Based on test from kernel/src/main.rs:1566

; Setup: 3 × 2 × 3 = 18 combinations
(foo 1) (foo 2) (foo 3)
(bar x) (bar y)
(baz P) (baz Q) (baz R)

; Test: Limit to first 7 results
(exec 0
  (, (foo $x) (bar $y) (baz $z))
  (O (head 7 (cux $z $y $x))))

; Expected output: First 7 combinations
; (cux P x 1)
; (cux P x 2)
; (cux P x 3)
; (cux P y 1)
; (cux P y 2)
; (cux P y 3)
; (cux Q x 1)
;
; Out of 18 possible combinations, only 7 are added to the space.
; The "head" sink limits the output (like SQL LIMIT or Unix head command).
;
; Syntax: (head <max-count> <template-to-instantiate>)
; - First argument: maximum number of results
; - Second argument: template to instantiate (like count, symbol name is arbitrary)
